      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-02-08_WidnesExaminer_art0021" n="art0021">
        <head>Sankey Sanatorium</head>
        <p>The Sankey Sanatorium</p>
        <p>- - CVIS reported at a meeting of the Haatrh C.Aomittee that tha Local Governmont Board required certain niteratioos be plane e th. Sanatorium at Sank.y,and it wan tret)hred that tho Chairman, Borough Surveyor 4;111 141,dical Offi-ier of Health be apnAnted to wait on the Local Govrlpment amrd to di.scuse the pr—posed al te ra ti on s. At a BOW qoent meetinv. thA report of th. deputation appointod to wait unon the Lne*l (Invert,. tn't B 'lard with reference to the proposed S.natorium Iva road, and the recommendations contained therein sl3Proord. Aickrudan SUTTON, in proposing tho acing i m of the</p>
        <p>minutes, said the suggested alterations were to his mind a great irnprovem.lnt upon the committee's proposals in the plans they sent up, and he thought they would result in them having a much better hospital than they had decided upon The new plans when re idy would be presented to the Council, and he thought the alterations would be carried out by adding very little to the cost of the building. The MLYOR aecondel, and the minutes were approved.</p>
