        <p>To make common Vegetables more inviting, always serve them with a good Corn Flour sauce. 19 make such a sauce simply mix a teaspoonful of good Corn Flour with teacupful of .milk, add a teaspoonful, of butter, and cook for three minutes. Try such a sauce with the commonest vegetables —turnips, arcots, onions, leeks, parsnips, &amp;c., and you will be convinced how much they are improved by it. For such a sauce good Corn Flour is essential, and the recognised best, owing to its great thickening power and delicate flavour is Brown &amp; Poison's "PATENT" Corn Flour Write to BROWN &amp; POISON, PAISLEY, enclosing a d. starn;), for their new booklet of simple recipes for dainty vegetable sauces.</p>
