        <p>VALUABLE 84101', DWELLING-HOUS itS AND GROUND MINTS IN WARRINGTON. TO BE SOLD BY AUCTION, By M. WILLIAM HICKhIAN. At the Blue Bell Inn, Horsemsrket-street, Warrington on Wednesday, the 13th day ot February. 1901, at 6 o'clock prompt, in the following or such other lots as may be deter- mined at the time of sale, and subject to the conditions of sale then to be produced : LOT those Four Messuages or DWELLING- HOUSES, situate and being Not 106, 108, 110, and 112. radgate-lane, Warrington, in the respective occupations of Messrs G Rigby, B Turley and others as tenants. Gross annual rental £7B. The property is held under a Lease, dated the 25th January 1899, for the term of 999 years from the Ist May, 1899, and will be sold subject to an apportioned yearly ground rent of £9 Is 3d. This is new property and is well and substantially built. It is ins good letting district, and affords an excellent oppor- tunity for small capitalists and others to acquire a sound property as a permanent investment. LOT that large and Commodious SHOP, with the yard and other conveniences thereto (formerly two shops), situate in the Market-place, Warrington, lately in the occupa- tion of Mr William MoCollom as tenant (there of, together with the right of way along a certain passage leading from Lyme-street to the rear of the said premises. The site comprises 126 square ya-ds or thereabouts. The property is held under a lease dated the 16th December, 1871, for the residue of a term of 99 years, from the let November 1871, at the yearly ground rent of IS 101: These premises are centrally situated, and are capable of ' being converted iato two shops; and are suitable for any business. LOT 3.—A1l those Leasehold improved YEARLY GROUND 1 RENTS, amounting in all to £4B 54, 4d., issuing out of nine several plots of land, situate in and near to John-street and Haydock-street. Warrington. The land is well covered by good and substantially built houses, and the district is a good letting one. For further particulars apply, as to Lot 1 to Mr Alfred Thompson, Bstate Agent, Mill-street, Warrington ' • as to Lot 2 to Mr F Womersley, Chartered Accountant, 1, Piccadilly. Manchester ; as to Lots 2 and 3 to Messrs Davies and For- thaw. Solicitors, 42, Sankey-street, Warrington; and as to all the Lots to the Auctioneer, Lyme-street. Warrington, or to THOMAS S STEEL, Solicitor, Mill-street Chambers, Warrington.</p>
